---
import SystemBandFigures from './SystemBandFigures.astro';
import changelog from '../../CHANGELOG.md?raw';
import { latestRelease } from '../lib/home/latest-release';
import { WINDOW_DAYS } from '../lib/ops/reads';
import { formatWindow } from '../lib/retention';

/**
 * The live system band on the home page (issue #437): the one place a visitor
 * who never opens /ops sees that this site is a running system in use.
 *
 * BUILT AT BUILD TIME EXCEPT FOR THE FIVE FIGURES. The frame, the release tile
 * and the fallback are prerendered with `/`; the figures are
 * src/components/SystemBandFigures.astro, deferred as a server island. The
 * release tile is the one tile that is a pure function of the commit, so it
 * has no reason to wait for a request, and building it here keeps it on the
 * page for a visitor without JavaScript.
 *
 * SIX CELLS BECAUSE SIX DIVIDES BY 1, 2 AND 3, the three column counts this
 * grid uses. index.astro's COLUMNS note has the rule: an empty track in a
 * `hairline-grid` paints as a block of rule colour rather than as nothing.
 */
const release = latestRelease(changelog);

/**
 * The fallback's labels, in the island's order. They have to match the
 * labels SystemBandFigures renders, or the swap moves a label from one cell to
 * another; tests/system-band.test.ts reads both.
 */
const LABELS = [
  'Public MCP tool calls',
  'Chat sessions',
  'Requests from agents',
  'Requests through the AI Gateway',
  'Requests that reached the Worker',
];

/** A tile's padding, the same as `OpsMetric`'s, so the fallback and the figure occupy one box. */
const CELL = 'bg-surface px-6 pb-7 pt-[26px]';
---

<section data-system-band aria-labelledby="system-band-heading" class="border-b border-rule">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-5 py-10 lg:px-10 lg:py-12">
    {/*
        The kicker and the link row copy "More writing" further down this
        page: the same quiet mono heading on the left and the same accent link
        on the right, so the band reads as a section of this page rather than a
        panel lifted from /ops. `data-system-band-links` is a container rather
        than the link itself because the how-it-works issue adds a second link
        to it.
      */}
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
      <h2 id="system-band-heading" class="font-mono text-micro uppercase text-ink-muted">
        Live · last {formatWindow(WINDOW_DAYS)}
      </h2>
      <div data-system-band-links class="flex flex-wrap gap-5">
        <a href="/ops#live-metrics" class="font-mono text-micro uppercase text-accent">
          All figures &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[70ch] text-body text-ink">
      Behind this writing runs a working system: an MCP server that AI agents call, and a chat agent
      that answers from what is published here.
    </p>

    {/*
        `auto-rows-fr` MAKES EVERY ROW AS TALL AS THE TALLEST, and that is
        what keeps the swap from moving a row. Measured in Chrome against
        `wrangler dev` on 2026-09-26: a fallback tile is 144px, and so is the
        release tile, but a live tile rendering its absence is 137px, because
        `OpsMetric`'s absent arm sets `text-heading` where the figure sets
        `text-figure`. Without this, a row of absences shrank by 7px when the
        island arrived. The release tile is built with the page and sits in
        the grid in both states, so it sets the floor at every breakpoint.
      */}
    <div class="hairline-grid mt-6 auto-rows-fr grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <SystemBandFigures server:defer>
        <Fragment slot="fallback">
          {/*
              NO FIGURE IN THE FALLBACK, AND THAT IS WHAT MAKES IT HONEST.
              This is what a visitor without JavaScript, a crawler and the AI
              Search index read, and a count baked in at build time would be a
              stale number presented as a live one. Each cell keeps its label
              and holds the figure's space empty: `h-[1lh]` on an element set
              in the figure's own type is exactly one line of that type, so
              the tile arriving does not move the label. The source line gets
              the same treatment for the same reason.
            */}
          {LABELS.map((label) => (
            <div data-band-fallback={label} class={CELL}>
              <p aria-hidden="true" class="h-[1lh] font-display text-figure" />
              <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">{label}</p>
              <p aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-[1lh] font-mono text-micro" />
            </div>
          ))}
        </Fragment>
      </SystemBandFigures>

      {/*
          The release tile, in `OpsMetric`'s three lines: the figure, what it
          is, where it came from. A DATE AND NEVER A TIME, which
          `recentReleases` already enforces (10 §1.4).

          THE ABSENCE HAS NO LINK. `latestRelease` returns `null` when the
          changelog has no `## ` heading or its first one does not parse,
          rather than falling through to an older release. A link built from
          a version that is not there would point at a release that does not
          exist, so the null arm is the same muted absence `OpsMetric`
          renders, in the same box.
        */}
      <div data-release-tile class="grid bg-surface">
        {release === null ? (
          <div class="px-6 pb-7 pt-[26px]">
            <p class="font-mono text-heading text-ink-muted">not available</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">Latest release</p>
            <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-micro text-ink-muted">
              CHANGELOG.md — the ops page says why
            </p>
          </div>
        ) : (
          <a href={release.url} class="block px-6 pb-7 pt-[26px] no-underline">
            <p class="font-display text-figure text-ink" data-numeric>
              {release.version}
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">
              Latest release · <time datetime={release.date}>{release.date}</time>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-micro text-ink-muted">CHANGELOG.md</p>
          </a>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
    {/*
        OUTSIDE THE ISLAND, AND PERMANENT. It sat in the fallback slot first,
        as a full-width grid row, and the row vanished when the figures
        arrived. Measured in Chrome against `wrangler dev` on 2026-09-26, band
        height before and after the swap: 572px to 489px at `lg`, 701px to
        611px at `md`, 1185px to 1052px at 500px wide, a shift of everything
        below the band on every page view with JavaScript. Its first wording
        opened with "These figures load after the page does", which was false
        for exactly the readers who never get them, a visitor without
        JavaScript and a crawler, so it now says only what is true in every
        state.
      */}
    <p data-band-note class="mt-4 text-small text-ink-muted">
      The live figures, and the system each one is read from, are always on the{' '}
      <a href="/ops#live-metrics">ops page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
